
========================================================================
  THE DEAD DROP
  High Tech, Low Lives: Ann at the Harborview drop
========================================================================
Seed: 1

== Seven Minutes Early ==
(Harborview Cafe, 06:47)

Three weeks since the feed went dark. You push through the door at 6:47,
seven minutes early. Protocol: never be the last person at a dead drop.

Three weeks of g0's protocols: text in dead image files, orders that are
not orders, cups that mean coordinates.

G0: Learn this. Prove you can do it. Then we talk about the Blackout.

Today's protocol. Order a double espresso, no sugar. Set it at the
corner table, handle to the window.

Check the cup three seats down. A stirrer across the rim means the
message is live. Photograph it with your student ID in frame. Leave.

Simple. Except Manager Chen is already here.

Chen, from Applied Systems. Your lecturer on Tuesdays and Thursdays, who
marks late arrivals in red.

She sits four tables away with a tablet and a cappuccino. You have never
seen her anywhere before 8:55.

The dead drop cup is three seats from her. Handle at four o'clock.
Stirrer across the rim. Live.

Exposure 1/6  Nerves 0/4  Systems 0/5

g0's file on you has one blank line. How do you work? [final]
  1. The Enforcer
     Chrome and muscle. Body +3.
  2. The Hacker
     The deck and the feed. Code +3.
> 1

Your chrome hand whirs as the door closes behind you. Steel under the
skin. You go through people and doors.

Exposure 1/6  Nerves 0/4  Systems 0/5  |  Role: enforcer

What do you take in first? Looking is free. [plan]
  1. The cameras
     No dice, no time. Find where the feed is blind.
  2. Nothing
     Trust the protocol.
> 1

Three cameras. One dead seat, behind the espresso machine. The feed
forgot it.
  | CH 1 DOOR: COVERED
  | CH 2 COUNTER: COVERED
  | CH 3 FLOOR: COVERED
  | SEAT 9, BEHIND MACHINE: NOT COVERED

Exposure 1/6  Nerves 0/4  Systems 0/5  |  Role: enforcer

What do you do? [plan]
  1. Proceed with the dead drop
     Make it look natural.
  2. Abort and sit with Chen
     Give up the drop. Hold on to your cover.
> 1

== Double Espresso ==
(Harborview Cafe, 06:49)

You step to the counter. The barista's nails click on the register
screen. She does not look up from her own feed.

ANN: Double espresso, no sugar.

Your voice is steady. The machine hisses. You count four heartbeats. Now
the register wants payment. Whatever you hand over, the feed will read.

Exposure 1/6  Nerves 0/4  Systems 0/5  |  Role: enforcer

How do you pay? [final]
  1. Tap the student card
     Names you: Ann Sho. Exposure +1.
  2. Pay in coins
     Names no one. Exposure +0.
  3. Show the Harker badge
     Names you: Sable Harker. Exposure +2.
> 2

Coins on scratched steel. The barista does not look up. The name field
stays black.
  | SUBJECT 1
  | NAME: ##########
  | SOURCE: NONE
  | CONF 38%

== Three Seats Down ==
(Harborview Cafe, 06:51)

The barista slides the cup across scratched steel. You carry it to the
corner table, the one with the peeling laminate. Handle to the window.
Exactly to protocol.

Now the hard part. The cup you must check is three seats down. Chen is
four tables away. She is reading, but she is *present*. One unnatural
glance and she will remember.

Your chrome hand is faster than the camera's frame rate. Between two
frames, a hand can do a lot.

You know the dead seat. It is on your way.

Exposure 1/6  Nerves 0/4  Systems 0/5  |  Role: enforcer  Identity
shown: Unnamed (cash)

Make the pass? [final]
  1. Palm the message past the camera
     4dF + Body (+3) vs 2
  2. Walk the blind line
     No roll. Needs the camera cones.
> 2

You cut behind the espresso machine, into the seat the cameras forgot.
The ID comes up. *Click.* Cup, stirrer and timestamp.

No camera saw you take it. Chen did not look up.

== Chen Stands ==
(Harborview Cafe, 07:02)

You sit. The espresso is bitter and cooling fast.

Chen gathers her tablet and coat. She stops at your table.

CHEN: Ann. Didn't expect to see you here this early.

ANN: Coffee before algorithms. Thought I'd try consciousness for once.

CHEN: Admirable. You always sit in corners?

The question lands odd. Weighted.

ANN: Better light. The window faces east.

Your chrome hand ticks as it cools. Chen's eyes rest on it a moment too
long.

Exposure 1/6  Nerves 0/4  Systems 0/5  |  Role: enforcer  Identity
shown: Unnamed (cash)  The drop: Clean

Chen is still in the room. Anything else? [final]
  1. Talk about the exam
     No change.
  2. Rest the chrome hand on the table, between her and the cup
     Exposure -1. Systems +1.
> 1

ANN: Is Thursday's exam on the whole term?

CHEN: On everything, Ann. It always is.

== Dead Image File ==
(Harborview Cafe, 07:09)

Chen is gone. The door chime rings once, and cold air follows it. Your
phone vibrates on the table.

A dead image file. You decode it in three seconds.

G0: Adequate. You completed the protocol under pressure.

G0: Campus mailbox tomorrow, 4 PM. We talk about the Blackout then.

G0: Cash. Old school. I approve.

G0: Your hand is good. Do not let it make you loud.

************************************************************************
  UNRESOLVED
************************************************************************

The feed closes the day with one person unnamed, or named and forgotten.
There is nothing to report.
  | SUBJECT 1: LOW EXPOSURE
  | EVENT: NONE
  | FLAG: NONE
  | FILE: CLOSED

You walk out into the early light. The mailbox is tomorrow, at four.
Whatever g0 tells you about the Blackout, the feed will not hear it
first.

THE END
Trail: arrive > counter > drop > table > phone > clean
r = play again, q = quit > q
Goodbye.
